## 5. Risks and mitigations

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Measurable trigger | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Legacy inventory database schema or access becomes unavailable | Medium | High: room searches may contain incomplete or incorrect data | Two consecutive synchronisation jobs fail, or imported data is more than 30 minutes old | Confirm schema and read-only credentials early; build an adapter and staging fixture; retain the last successful room snapshot; alert staff when data is stale |
| Facilities iCal feeds are malformed, delayed or semantically inconsistent | Medium | High: availability could be wrong | Feed parsing failure rate exceeds 1% or feed age exceeds 30 minutes | Validate and quarantine bad feeds; retain last known valid schedule; create per-campus feed configuration; provide a manual staff override and operational alert |
| Concurrent reservations cause double booking | Medium | Very high | Any integration/concurrency test observes two accepted overlapping reservations for one room | Enforce conflict checks in a database transaction with appropriate exclusion/locking constraints; perform concurrency tests at release gates; return `409 Conflict` on rejected races |
| Search performance fails at semester start | Medium | High | Load test or production search p95 exceeds 400 ms for ten minutes | Pre-load test with 2,000 users; add indexes and query budgets; synchronise external data locally; cache stable metadata; scale application instances and tune connection pools |
| Kiosk updates are delayed or kiosks display misleading data | Medium | Medium/High | More than 1% of changes are not visible within ten seconds, or kiosk cache is older than the agreed threshold | Use transactional outbox with retries; support polling fallback; store last-known schedule locally; display update age and offline status; monitor per-room delivery |
| SAML configuration or claims differ between environments | Medium | High: users cannot log in or receive incorrect roles | Authentication failure rate exceeds 2%, or role-mapping contract tests fail | Obtain test IdP metadata early; automate configuration validation; use contract tests; fail closed for unknown roles; maintain an emergency staff support procedure |
| Notification provider outage causes missing reminders | Medium | Medium | Notification queue age exceeds five minutes or delivery failure exceeds 2% | Use an outbox and retry with exponential backoff; make messages idempotent; monitor provider responses; allow a second provider or manual export as a contingency |
| Two-person team cannot safely operate the system | Medium | High | A staging rollback takes more than ten minutes, or a production task requires undocumented manual steps | Automate deployment and rollback; maintain runbooks; use health checks and dashboards; practise restoration and rollback monthly; keep the first release as one deployable |
| New-campus onboarding requires code changes | Low/Medium | Medium | A test campus cannot be configured and imported without modifying application code | Represent campus, opening hours, time zone, equipment and external endpoints as validated configuration; create an onboarding checklist and configuration acceptance test |
| Privacy or audit requirements are violated by logs | Low/Medium | High | Automated log scan finds email patterns, names or tokens in application logs | Central redaction middleware; structured logging allow-list; secret scanning and privacy tests in CI; restrict audit-log access and review retention policies |

---

## 6. Open questions for the product owner

1. What exact definition of “48 hours’ notice” applies to recurring block bookings: 48 hours before creation, before each occurrence, or before the first occurrence?
2. When a block booking overrides student reservations, should CLRS automatically cancel those reservations and issue notifications, or should staff confirm each affected reservation?
3. What are the official campus time zones and daylight-saving rules?
4. How fresh must iCal and room-inventory data be before the system marks it as stale?
5. Should equipment be reserved independently from rooms, or is equipment only a room-search attribute?
6. What are the retention periods and access rules for staff audit records and utilisation reports?
7. Which email and push providers are approved, and what delivery guarantees or rate limits do they provide?
8. What is the required kiosk authentication mechanism, and how should a kiosk be provisioned or revoked?
9. Is server-sent events acceptable for kiosks, or is polling required because of campus network restrictions?
10. Should users be allowed to create multiple reservations whose combined duration is exactly three hours, and how are cancelled or overridden bookings counted?
11. What is the expected monthly reservation volume and the maximum number of kiosks for capacity planning?
12. What availability window should be used for synthetic monitoring when a campus has exceptional opening hours or holidays?

